        <p>"Maybe," Betsy said, though she didn't look convinced. The weight of the secret, though, felt lighter now that she had shared it.</p>
        <p>"Listen to me, Betsy," Carla said, leaning forward, looking the teenager dead in the eye. Her tone was sincere. "You are sixteen years old. You shouldn't have to be the referee in your parents' marriage. And you definitely shouldn't be the one carrying the emotional weight of your mother's recovery."</p>
